# Static files and add-ons

- `internal/utils`, `internal/extract` and `internal/docker/static_addons.go` are legacy library code kept compiling but **not wired to any HTTP route**. Task C implements the planned `/api/v1/static` routes (types in `internal/apitypes/host.go`) on top of the data directory's `static/` (`datadir.Layout.Static()`); `utils.StaticDir` still points at the old working-directory path and must not be used by new code.
- Extraction rules to preserve: empty or `.` `extract_to` means the build-context root; root extraction stages entries and rejects collisions without overwriting; never trust archive entry paths; nested archives are not expanded.
- Verify with `go test ./internal/extract/... ./internal/utils/... ./internal/docker/...`.
